{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778614085517,"sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"functions.bash:9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'id: MONDO:777' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo | grep -oP 'MONDO:777\\d+' | sort -t: -k2 -n | tail -5","description":"Find highest MONDO 777 ID"},"output":"MONDO:7770008\nMONDO:7770008\nMONDO:7770009\nMONDO:7770010\nMONDO:7770011\n","metadata":{"output":"MONDO:7770008\nMONDO:7770008\nMONDO:7770009\nMONDO:7770010\nMONDO:7770011\n","exit":0,"description":"Find highest MONDO 777 ID","truncated":false},"title":"Find highest MONDO 777 ID","time":{"start":1778614085513,"end":1778614085516}},"id":"prt_e1da92185001dkMjD1DjDZODLS","sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","messageID":"msg_e1da91215001sbKEdI5320YeVD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778614086493,"sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"functions.bash:10","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'predisposition' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo | grep -i medulloblastoma","description":"Search for medulloblastoma predisposition"},"output":"def: \"Inherited cancer-predisposing syndrome due to biallelic BRCA2 mutations is a rare cancer-predisposing syndrome, associated with the D1 subgroup of Fanconi anemia (FA), characterized by progressive bone marrow failure, cardiac, brain, intestinal or skeletal abnormalities and predisposition to various malignancies. Bone marrow suppression and the incidence of developmental abnormalities are less frequent than in other FA, but cancer risk is very high with the spectrum of childhood cancers including Wilms tumor, brain tumor (often medulloblastoma) and ALL/AML.\" [Orphanet:319462]\ndef: \"A neoplastic syndrome most often caused by mutations in the hSNF5/INI1 tumor suppressor gene. It is characterized by the development of an atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumor in infancy and early childhood. This highly aggressive tumor develops in the central nervous system as an isolated lesion or in combination with extrarenal or renal rhabdoid tumor. Patients may also develop other central nervous system malignancies including medulloblastoma, supratentorial primitive neuroectodermal tumor, and choroid plexus carcinoma.\" [NCIT:C93268]\n","metadata":{"output":"def: \"Inherited cancer-predisposing syndrome due to biallelic BRCA2 mutations is a rare cancer-predisposing syndrome, associated with the D1 subgroup of Fanconi anemia (FA), characterized by progressive bone marrow failure, cardiac, brain, intestinal or skeletal abnormalities and predisposition to various malignancies. Bone marrow suppression and the incidence of developmental abnormalities are less frequent than in other FA, but cancer risk is very high with the spectrum of childhood cancers including Wilms tumor, brain tumor (often medulloblastoma) and ALL/AML.\" [Orphanet:319462]\ndef: \"A neoplastic syndrome most often caused by mutations in the hSNF5/INI1 tumor suppressor gene. It is characterized by the development of an atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumor in infancy and early childhood. This highly aggressive tumor develops in the central nervous system as an isolated lesion or in combination with extrarenal or renal rhabdoid tumor. Patients may also develop other central nervous system malignancies including medulloblastoma, supratentorial primitive neuroectodermal tumor, and choroid plexus carcinoma.\" [NCIT:C93268]\n","exit":0,"description":"Search for medulloblastoma predisposition","truncated":false},"title":"Search for medulloblastoma predisposition","time":{"start":1778614086489,"end":1778614086492}},"id":"prt_e1da92765001Dscl9WzR5pV0oB","sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","messageID":"msg_e1da91215001sbKEdI5320YeVD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778614087515,"sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"functions.bash:11","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'susceptibility' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo | grep -i medulloblastoma","description":"Search for medulloblastoma susceptibility"},"output":"name: medulloblastoma\ndef: \"A malignant, invasive embryonal neoplasm arising from the cerebellum. It occurs predominantly in children and has the tendency to metastasize via the cerebrospinal fluid pathways. Signs and symptoms include truncal ataxia, disturbed gait, lethargy, headache, and vomiting. There are four histologic variants: classic medulloblastoma, large cell/anaplastic medulloblastoma, desmoplastic/nodular medulloblastoma, and medulloblastoma with extensive nodularity.\" [NCIT:C3222]\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma\" EXACT [DOID:0050902, MONDO:Lexical, NCIT:C3222, OMIM:155255, Orphanet:616] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma with extensive nodularity\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, autosomal recessive, autosomal dominant, somatic mutation\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, desmoplastic\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, desmoplastic, autosomal recessive, autosomal dominant, somatic mutation\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, malignant\" EXACT [NCIT:C3222]\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, somatic\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastomas\" EXACT [NCIT:C3222]\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/cerebellar_medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: seeAlso \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/7005/medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"GARD:0007005\"}\n","metadata":{"output":"name: medulloblastoma\ndef: \"A malignant, invasive embryonal neoplasm arising from the cerebellum. It occurs predominantly in children and has the tendency to metastasize via the cerebrospinal fluid pathways. Signs and symptoms include truncal ataxia, disturbed gait, lethargy, headache, and vomiting. There are four histologic variants: classic medulloblastoma, large cell/anaplastic medulloblastoma, desmoplastic/nodular medulloblastoma, and medulloblastoma with extensive nodularity.\" [NCIT:C3222]\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma\" EXACT [DOID:0050902, MONDO:Lexical, NCIT:C3222, OMIM:155255, Orphanet:616] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma with extensive nodularity\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, autosomal recessive, autosomal dominant, somatic mutation\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, desmoplastic\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, desmoplastic, autosomal recessive, autosomal dominant, somatic mutation\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, malignant\" EXACT [NCIT:C3222]\nsynonym: \"medulloblastoma, somatic\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"medulloblastomas\" EXACT [NCIT:C3222]\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/cerebellar_medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: seeAlso \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/7005/medulloblastoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"GARD:0007005\"}\n","exit":0,"description":"Search for medulloblastoma susceptibility","truncated":false},"title":"Search for medulloblastoma susceptibility","time":{"start":1778614087511,"end":1778614087513}},"id":"prt_e1da92b92001ln9w6KQUVzqpkQ","sessionID":"ses_1e25759a7ffenVC9nmfitzkS1E","messageID":"msg_e1da91215001sbKEdI5320YeVD"}}
